| `u = - gPos·x - gVel·ẋ` | When the pole is balanced, a proportional‑derivative (PD) controller on the cart position gently recenters the cart while damping its motion. The `gVel` term prevents the cart from overshooting the centre. |
| Wall‑avoidance (`|x| > wall`) | As soon as the cart gets within ~0.15 m of the ±2.4 m limits we force a push *away* from the wall. This eliminates the “default‑right” drift that caused the last failure. |
| Keep the original tilt‑error branch unchanged | The logs already prove that `θ + 0.9θ̇` with a 0.012 threshold is the most reliable way to react to a falling pole. |

