| **Small pole error** | First checks the walls, then applies a *very* gentle “pull‑to‑center” (K_x ≈ 0.15). | The pole is already stable; we only need to keep the cart from drifting into a wall. The gains are small enough that the cart drifts slowly, giving the pole plenty of time to stay upright. |
| **Bias** (`bias = 0.0` or a tiny positive number) | Optional right‑bias can be used to keep the cart a little away from the left wall (empirically the right side is a bit more forgiving). | In the original runs the cart tended to spend a lot of time near the left wall; a tiny bias moves the “resting point” toward the centre‑right, reducing the chance of hitting the left wall. |

