* **Dead‑zone (`TH = 0.012`)** prevents chattering when the pole is already balanced; the controller stays idle (or uses the harmless default) instead of repeatedly applying opposite forces.
* **Cart‑position safety** is only triggered when the cart is dangerously close to the limits (|x| > 2 m). This avoids the slow drift observed when the safety rule is evaluated first.
* **Neutral fallback** chooses the same default direction that the successful 500‑step runs used (action = 2). Because the cart is already near the centre, this default does not push it out of the safe region.

