#### Observations from the 20‑step logs  

*When the pole is far from vertical* (`|θ+0.9·θ̇| > 0.013`) the chosen action always matches the sign of the combined term (`c`).  
The logs show exactly that:

```
c = θ + 0.9·θ̇
c > 0  → action 2 (push right)
c < 0  → action 1 (push left)
```

The resulting state moves the pole back toward the upright region in the next step (the angle changes sign or gets smaller).

*When the pole is almost upright* (`|c| ≤ 0.013`) the cart drifts slowly left/right.  
