### 4. Proposed refined rule set  

Even though S‑3 already hits 500/500, a few tiny tweaks can make the policy more robust to measurement noise and to future variations (different pole length, friction, etc.):

| Rule | Rationale |
|------|-----------|
| **1️⃣ Angle‑dominant** – Compute `A = θ + K₁·ω` with `K₁ = 0.9`. If `|A| > τ₁` (`τ₁ = 0.013`) → push opposite the sign of `A`. | Keeps the pole upright; the same combination that worked best. |
| **2️⃣ Position‑dead‑zone** – If `|A| ≤ τ₁` then look at the cart position **only** (ignore velocity). Use a slightly larger dead‑zone `τ₂ = 0.06 m`. | Prevents the controller from “chasing” micro‑movements while still pulling the cart back before it reaches the ±2.4 m limits. |
| **3️⃣ Position‑correction** – When `|x| > τ₂` → push **toward the centre** (`action = 1` if `x>0`, else `action = 2`). | Directly recenters the cart. |
| **4️⃣ Tie‑break** – If `|x| ≤ τ₂` (i.e. perfectly centred) → use the sign of the cart velocity **as a gentle damping**: <br> if `v > 0.02` → push left (1); <br> if `v < -0.02` → push right (2); <br> otherwise push right (2) (deterministic fallback). | The velocity‑aware tie‑break damps drift without introducing random behaviour; the fallback keeps the policy deterministic. |
| **5️⃣ Safety clip** – After choosing an action, optionally check the predicted next position (using the known physics step) and forbid an action that would immediately violate the ±2.4 m bound. | Guarantees no “instant death” due to a bad tie‑break. |

