**Pseudo‑code**

```text
// constants
K_omega   = 0.85          // weight on angular velocity
DEAD_ZONE = 0.015         // radians
POS_ZONE  = 0.06          // metres
VEL_MAX   = 0.5           // m/s (optional damping)

// inputs (from observation)
x      = state[0]   // cart position
x_dot  = state[1]   // cart velocity
theta  = state[2]   // pole angle
theta_dot = state[3] // pole angular velocity

// 1) primary pole‑balance term
phi = theta + K_omega * theta_dot

if (abs(phi) > DEAD_ZONE) {
    // pole is leaning → push opposite direction
    if (phi > 0) action = 2   // push right
    else          action = 1   // push left
}
else {
    // 2) pole is almost upright → keep cart centred
    if (abs(x) > POS_ZONE) {
        if (x > 0) action = 1   // cart too far right → push left
        else       action = 2   // cart too far left  → push right
    }
    else {
        // 3) we are inside both dead‑zones → use deterministic centre‑bias
        if (x > 0)   action = 1
        else if (x < 0) action = 2
        else {
