| Randomised tie‑break (alternating left/right) | Removes any hidden bias if the environment were asymmetric. | No measurable benefit on the classic CartPole; keep deterministic for reproducibility. |

**6. Bottom line**

The **three‑rule hierarchy** (pole‑first → position‑fallback → deterministic tie‑break) already yields perfect performance on the benchmark (500 / 500). Keep the thresholds as shown, and you will consistently keep the pole upright for the maximum allowed 500 time steps.
