### 3. Updated rule set (final version)

```text
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Constants (tuned from the successful runs)
K_omega   = 0.9          # weight for angular velocity
THETA_DEAD = 0.013       # angular error dead‑zone (rad)
X_DEAD     = 0.025       # cart‑position dead‑zone (m) – tighter than before
# -----------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. Compute the combined error that captures pole tilt & speed
e = theta + K_omega * omega   # theta = pole angle, omega = angular velocity

# 2. Primary decision – if the pole is moving away from vertical, act immediately
IF |e| > THETA_DEAD THEN
    IF e > 0 THEN
        action = 2          # push right → counter‑clockwise tilt
    ELSE
        action = 1          # push left  → clockwise tilt
    ENDIF

# 3. Secondary decision – pole is almost upright, keep the cart centred
