### 3. Updated (and slightly refined) rule set  

Below is the final policy that should be used from now on.  
Only two thresholds are needed; they are kept exactly as the empirical optimum showed, but I add a tiny safety margin (0.001 rad) to avoid numerical edge cases.

```text
# -------------------------------------------------
#  CART‑POLE BALANCING POLICY (deterministic)
# -------------------------------------------------
#   State variables
#     x   – cart position   (m)   –2.4 … 2.4
#     v   – cart velocity   (m/s) (unused)
#     θ   – pole angle      (rad) –0.2095 … 0.2095
#     ω   – pole angular velocity (rad/s) (unused)
#
#   Composite error term
#     e = θ + 0.9 * ω
#
#   Thresholds
#     T_θ = 0.013      # angular‑error magnitude that requires immediate correction
#     T_x = 0.05       # cart‑position dead‑zone
#
#   Action mapping (discrete)
#     1 → push left   (negative force)
#     2 → push right  (positive force)
#
# -------------------------------------------------
#  Decision logic
# -------------------------------------------------
IF |e| > T_θ THEN
    # Pole is tipping – fight the tip direction
    IF e > 0      → action = 2   # push right
    ELSE          → action = 1   # push left
ELSE
    # Pole is essentially upright – keep cart centred
    IF x >  T_x   → action = 1   # cart too far right → push left
    ELIF x < -T_x → action = 2   # cart too far left  → push right
    ELSE          → action = 2   # exactly centred (or inside dead‑zone) → deterministic right
```

