### Updated, compact rule set  

Below is the final policy that consistently reaches the 500‑step limit. It is expressed in plain pseudocode so you can copy‑paste it into the next experiment.

```text
// constants (tuned from the experiments)
K        = 0.9          // weight for angular velocity
THRESH   = 0.013        // dead‑band for the combined angle term
POS_DEAD = 0.05         // cart‑position dead‑band (meters)

// state variables (provided each step)
x   = cart position          // -4.8 … 4.8
theta = pole angle           // -0.418 … 0.418   (radians)
omega = pole angular velocity// -∞ … ∞

// 1️⃣  angle‑plus‑scaled‑velocity test
combo = theta + K * omega

if (abs(combo) > THRESH) {
    // pole is outside the tiny stability cone → act on its direction
    if (combo > 0) {
        action = 2   // push right
    } else {
