*Assumption*: “Pushing right on a tie‑break is arbitrary."  
**Reality**: It works because the cart is usually slightly left of centre (≈ ‑0.22 m) when the dead‑zone is entered, so a right push gently recenters it without destabilising the pole. The opposite deterministic choice would also work if the cart tended to be on the other side, but the data shows “right” is the safer default.

