### 4️⃣ Updated rule set (the one we will keep)  

Below is the final, compact policy that consistently reaches the 500‑step limit.  
All constants were tuned by looking at the successful trace above and by a quick grid search on the few remaining failure modes.

```text
# -------------------------------------------------
#  CART‑POLE BALANCING POLICY (deterministic)
# -------------------------------------------------
# 1. Compute the combined angle‑velocity term
p = theta + 0.9 * omega

# 2. Main decision
if abs(p) > 0.013:                # pole is noticeably tilted
    if p > 0:                     # tilting left → push right
        action = 2                # push right
    else:                         # tilting right → push left
        action = 1                # push left
else:                             # pole is almost upright
    # 3. Position‑correction dead‑band
    if x > 0.05:                   # cart too far right → push left
        action = 1
    elif x < -0.05:                # cart too far left → push right
        action = 2
    else:                         # cart essentially centred
        # deterministic tie‑break – choose right (any fixed direction works)
        action = 2
# -------------------------------------------------
```

